{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then ndim(v_1) ≠ ndim(v_2) ∨ shape(v_1, 0) ≠ shape(v_2, 0)
>>
Rule 133 (Number of dimensions must be less than 3, minimum tensor value is always greater than 0.)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) < 3 ∧ min(v_1) > 0
>>
Rule 134 (The dimensions of a tensor is same as elements count of tuple and max value of tensor must be smaller than 1.)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tuple(int)} |= ndim(v_1) = v_2.len ∧ max(v_1) < 1
>>
Rule 135 (Tuple can only contains int32 or int64.)
{v_1: tuple(dtype)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : v_1[i] = 3 ∨ v_1[i] = 4
>>
Rule 136 (If a tensor is a 1x1 tensor, then it must have dtype int8)
{v_1: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) = 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) = 1 then dtype_(v_1) = 1
>>
Rule 137 (If a tensor has at least 2 dimensions then, product of dimensions should be less than some constant number)
{v_1: tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) > 1 then (shape(v_1, 0) * shape(v_1, 1)) < v_2
>>
Rule 138 (If dimension of the tensor is equal to constant, then min and max value must be greater than 0.)
{v_1: tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) = v_2 then min(v_1) > 0 ∧ max(v_1) > 0
>>
Rule 139 (The shape of two tensors at dimensions 0 and 1 are same.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0) ∧ shape(v_1, 1) = shape(v_2, 1)
>>
Rule 140 (Dtype can only be int8 or float64.)
{v_1: tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8
